abstract: >
  Compact derived datasets and the complete analysis pipeline for an open,
  transferable environmental-justice method that prioritises school-level
  air-pollution protection in data-scarce cities, demonstrated across six
  Central Asian capitals (Tashkent, Almaty, Astana, Bishkek, Dushanbe,
  Ashgabat) and transferred out-of-region (Accra, Kathmandu, Lima).

  The archive includes the reference-anchoring procedure for municipal
  low-cost networks, the school-level exposure and equity layers, and the
  validation outputs. Code is MIT; data derivatives are CC-BY-4.0.

  The DOI above is the concept DOI and always resolves to the latest
  version; version 2.1.0 is 10.5281/zenodo.21824161.

